  "description": "like this bike: At 37 lbs.\nit's a bit full-figured. We admit it. But it's got a lot more than a nice\npersonality on the plus side, so hear me out. For starters, the Discovery\n1 has the same great frame design, rear suspension pivot point and sealed\nbearings as its Discovery series siblings. The difference is it's made\nentirely of steel which is strong and durable, but not terribly light.\n\nIf you're considering this bike, you've no doubt been tempted by the discount\ndepartment store lookalikes. Don't do it. The Discovery 1 is a real bike\nassembled by a professional mechanic at a Fuji dealer, not a toy assembled\nby some unskilled kid. The way a bike is assembled plays a critical role\nin how well it works (obviously) but also in how long it lasts. Improperly\nadjusted bearings wear out quickly. Insufficiently tightened crank arms\nwork loose and self-destruct. And no matter how much money you save, the\ncheap imitation won't weigh any less than ours.\n\nThe Discovery 1 also comes equipped with 7-speed shifting that features\na super-low climbing gear. So what's not to love? If you really want to\nbe a hero, consider one for a deserving kid at holiday or graduation time.\nYou won't hear any complaints. We're sure.",
